>Gosh!  There's so many possibilities...

No kidding.  One thing I played with is to have stethescopes allow
you to listen at doors; it seemed like the most obvious application for
them.  I have coded this into nethack on my machine, and it works great.
If you're at a closed/locked door; you can apply the stethescope to
a door; you may hear whether there's anything on the other side.  If its
a simple space on the other side (ie. a #), it tells you if you hear
anything in that space (maybe...).  If its a room on the other side,
any awake monster in the room make a "rustling noise" (maybe...).  The
maybe is that you may not listen closely enough (20% chance) and so
miss the sounds.  I'd like to tie listening capabilities to intelligence
and lick, but haven't yet.
